	'br_more' => 'About the studio',
	'br_p1' => 'Renata Solberg spent twelve years cooking on hot lines before founding Mise Studio in 2014. Too many commercial kitchens are drawn around equipment catalogues, with ranges and fryers dropped wherever standard dimensions fit rather than where cooks actually stand. When a room ignores the reality of service, line cooks spend their shifts dodging hot doors, reaching across each other and losing minutes at the peak of an order. We draw around the working brigade instead.',
	'br_p2' => 'Every project starts on site between services, in the quiet hours from 09:30 to 11:30 or from 15:00 to 17:00. Over two hours we trace your brigade\'s real walking routes, talk through the menu and the covers, and note what the building already fixes: the gas, water, drainage and power that are in the walls. The drawings that follow then reflect the room you have, not a tidy ideal.',
	'br_p3' => 'Within five working days of the visit you receive a written brief covering covers, menu, brigade size, rooms and services on site. Every drawing after it is checked against that page. And before your contractor orders a single range, we tape the layout at full scale on your floor so your brigade can walk it.',
