	'pv_b1' => 'Mise Studio collects personal information necessary to organize kitchen site visits, prepare written briefs, coordinate contractor drawings, and manage client accounts. When you submit a booking or contact inquiry, we record your name, business name, site location, email address, and phone number. This information is used exclusively by studio manager Mina Castell and our design team to correspond with you, conduct site visits, and prepare project documentation. We do not sell, rent, or distribute personal information to external commercial marketing platforms or advertising networks.',
	'pv_b2' => 'All project records and correspondence are stored securely on our studio systems at Unit 4, Ferrier Yard, 22 Canal Street, Oldmere. If you subscribe to our visit waitlist, your email address is retained solely to notify you of available appointment windows or new monthly calendar releases. You have the right to request a summary of the personal information we hold about you, or to request the complete deletion of your records from our systems at any time by emailing hello@mise-studio.example.',
	'pv_hh1' => 'Information we collect and purpose of use',
	'pv_hh2' => 'Data retention, waitlist records, and client rights',
	'pv_intro' => 'This privacy policy outlines how Mise Studio handles your personal information when you contact our studio or book a site visit. We protect your data and never share your details with outside parties.',
	'pv_title' => 'Privacy',
	'rm2_b1' => 'Where the heat is: ranges, plancha, and fryers aligned under one continuous canopy, and the pass the plates leave from. We measure critical clearances across the cooking line, maintaining a 1,050 mm hot aisle so two line cooks can pass safely without crossing behind hot fryers. We check extraction canopy overhangs to capture grease and heat, evaluate range blocks against menu volumes, and position plating passes with integrated heat lamps. The height and width of the pass are calibrated so service staff collect dishes without leaning over hot equipment or crowding line cooks.',
	'rm2_b2' => 'Where the morning goes: long stainless benches, a cool bench for pastry, and cold rooms you can reach with full hands. We measure 900 mm prep aisle clearances to provide ample room for vegetable chopping and butchery while keeping under-bench storage accessible. The pastry bench is specified with a smooth stone surface set under natural window light, positioned well away from front-of-house coffee queues and hot cooking lines. Walk-in cold room shelving heights and aisle widths are calculated so cooks can carry loaded crates through heavy insulated doors without obstruction.',
	'rm2_b3' => 'Where trolleys travel: deliveries in one door, dirty plates out another, and dry stores in between. We map the physical journey of every delivery crate and soiled plate to prevent hygiene cross-contamination. Wash-up areas feature pass-through dishwashers, pre-rinse overhead sprays, and generous soiled sorting tabling. Goods-in routes from external delivery doors directly access dry store shelving and walk-in refrigeration. We measure trolley widths, door clearance swings, and corridor turning circles to ensure delivery dollies and dish return trolleys never collide in tight passages during busy service hours.',
	'rm2_cap1' => 'Every room a plate passes through',
	'rm2_cap2' => 'From the hot line to the goods-in door.',
	'rm2_h' => 'Three groups of rooms',
	'rm2_intro' => 'A brief covers every room a plate or delivery passes through, establishing ergonomic clearances and linear routes. We look at equipment footprints, service connections, and brigade movement across three core areas.',
	'rm2_m1' => '1,050 mm between the line and the pass, so two cooks pass without touching.',
	'rm2_m1l' => 'Hot aisle',
	'rm2_m2' => '900 mm between benches, with under-bench storage still reachable.',
	'rm2_m2l' => 'Prep aisle',
	'rm2_m3' => 'Trolley widths, door swings and corridor turning circles from goods-in to wash-up.',
	'rm2_m3l' => 'Trolley routes',
	'rm2_m4' => 'Overhang and extraction over every cooking appliance.',
	'rm2_m4l' => 'Canopy',
	'rm2_mh' => 'What is measured',
	'rm2_nb' => 'Mise Studio specialises strictly in back-of-house commercial kitchen architecture, brigade ergonomics, and services coordination. A kitchen brief does not cover front-of-house furniture for dining rooms, customer bar design, dining lighting schemes, or exterior restaurant signage. By focusing exclusively on the rooms behind the pass where food is prepared, stored, and washed, we ensure that every square metre of kitchen space is engineered for hygiene, safety, culinary speed, and durable workflow without distraction.',
