	'stp_sh' => 'Three stages: Tape, Walk, and Adjust',
	'su_b1' => 'Renata Solberg founded Mise Studio in 2014 after spending twelve years cooking on commercial hot lines. Throughout more than a decade in restaurant kitchens, she watched owners order equipment straight from manufacturer catalogues without considering how cooks actually move between ranges and sinks. The studio began when Renata sketched her first kitchen layout directly on a café floor using children\'s chalk during quiet morning hours, testing clearances with the chef before any building work began. That initial test established our core philosophy: kitchens must be drawn around the brigade, not around catalogue pages. Today, after drawing 118 kitchens for restaurants, hotels, schools, and bakeries, every project still begins with quiet observation and ends with a full-scale test before a single piece of equipment is ordered.',
	'su_b2' => 'Our design methodology rests on three practical standards that prevent expensive mistakes. First, we visit your site exclusively during the quiet gap between services, either 09:30–11:30 or 15:00–17:00, when your brigade has time to talk without interrupting customers. Second, we deliver one concise written brief within five working days that records covers, menu requirements, brigade numbers, and existing wall services. Third, we tape every proposed layout at full scale on your floor so your cooks can walk a simulated service before your contractor orders a range.',
	'su_b4' => 'The studio follows a disciplined daily routine from Monday to Friday. At 08:30 the studio opens for drawing work and contractor technical coordination. From 09:30 to 11:30 we conduct morning site visits in the gap between breakfast and lunch service. At 13:00 the team gathers for collective drawing reviews and layout revisions. Between 15:00 and 17:00 we run afternoon site visits or floor-tape tests with brigades after lunch service finishes. The studio closes at 17:30. We are closed on weekends and public holidays, and we answer all emails within one working day.',
